+# Request spec profiling and execution defaults
+
+## Scope
+
+This phase follows `model-spec-performance.md`. Only request spec configuration
+and setup change. No application code, factories, existing assertions, system
+specs or streaming specs change. Existing exclusions remain in effect.
+
+## Reproduce (one directory, no parallelization)
+
+```sh
+docs/profile-requests.sh normal
+TEST_STACK_PROF=1 docs/profile-requests.sh sampled
+SEED=67890 docs/profile-requests.sh another-seed
+bundle exec stackprof tmp/request-profile/sampled/stack-prof-report-wall-total.dump --text --limit 30
+```
+
+The script only runs `bundle exec rspec spec/requests`. Outputs are saved in
+`tmp/request-profile/<label>/`: RSpec JSON/progress, timing and a slow-example
+summary, plus an optional TestProf/StackProf dump. Use a new label per run.
+Sampling uses wall time at 10 ms without raw stacks (see the model-phase notes
+about memory limits). Do not run multiple directories together.
+
+## Baseline provenance
+
+The prior phase's available notes/artifacts contain a model baseline but **no
+request baseline**. The request baseline here was captured before making any
+request changes, with the existing model improvements still in place. Those
+improvements were model-type scoped; the stray verbose-query assignment was in
+a model spec file, which is not loaded by a standalone request run. Thus the
+standalone request setup still had its original inline workers and ordinary SQL
+logging. Do not compare this to a combined whole-suite baseline that also loaded
+the old verbose-query assignment.
+
+Same environment as the model phase: Ruby 4.0.6, Rails 8.1.3.1, RSpec 3.13,
+Sidekiq 8.1.6, local PostgreSQL/Redis; CI and COVERAGE unset. Seed 12345 unless
+otherwise stated. These are local measurements, not absolute CI timings.
+
+| Run | Examples | Failures | RSpec execution | Process wall |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| Baseline, sampled | 1,877 | 0 | 170.953s | 174.736s |
+| Fake jobs + initial integration tags, sampled diagnostic | 1,877 | 2 | 130.720s | 134.246s |
+| Shared cache setup + corrected tags, sampled | 1,877 | 0 | 118.068s | 121.568s |
+| Scoped routes/logs, sampled | 1,877 | 0 | 97.745s | 101.345s |
+| Final + setup regressions, no profiler | 1,887 | 0 | 95.069s | 99.691s |
+| Seed 67890 + isolation probes, no profiler | 1,887 | 0 | 94.206s | 98.107s |
+
+## Findings and changes
+
+### Inline callbacks were amplifying setup
+
+The baseline sampled about 60% in fabrication and 28% in Sidekiq enqueueing /
+inline execution (inclusive percentages overlap). `TriggerWebhookWorker` alone
+accounted for about 21%, even though these requests do not test webhooks.
+
+Request examples now use a **block-scoped fake Sidekiq mode** by default. Jobs
+are genuinely enqueued/serialized, not stubbed away. The existing rspec-sidekiq
+hook clears queues before each example. Other spec types retain their previous
+defaults, including the earlier model optimizations.
+
+Use `:inline_jobs` when assertions or setup need workers' effects. Tags retain
+real processing for media uploads, service-generated notifications/conversations,
+home/list timelines, unfavouriting, report email, and account-action email.
+Negative email cases in admin confirmations/change-email also remain inline so
+that their assertions cannot pass merely because email jobs never ran. The two
+diagnostic failures were the unfavourite integration cases; their assertions
+were **not** changed, and the whole unfavourite group now runs inline.
+
+Old global `Sidekiq.testing!(:fake)` calls in examples were replaced by
+`inline_jobs: false` metadata. This is inherited, can override an inline parent,
+and cannot leak global state or be silently masked by a thread-local mode.
+Do not nest Sidekiq block-mode changes inside examples (Sidekiq disallows this);
+use metadata instead. The explicit fake block in `before_all` runs outside the
+per-example block.
+
+### Cache-policy matrix rebuilt identical records 258 times
+
+`cache_spec.rb` took 35.140s of the baseline. Its common database graph is now
+built once with TestProf's **transactional `before_all`**, not plain RSpec
+`before(:all)`. Rails still opens/rolls back a transaction per example, and
+TestProf rolls back the outer setup transaction after the group. The existing
+`let` lookups fetch fresh records rather than sharing mutable AR instances.
+
+Requests, sign-ins, settings, headers, and all assertions still run for each of the 258
+cases. Redis and Rails cache cleanup remain per-example; neither is shared as a
+substitute for database isolation. The final matrix takes about 4.1s. This is a
+setup lifecycle change only; no factory definitions were changed.
+
+### Temporary routes reloaded the entire app after each signature example
+
+The signature-verification group previously drew temporary routes and reloaded
+all application routes 30 times. It now draws temporary routes once before the
+group and restores real routes once afterward. The fake controller is still
+stubbed/restored per example, and time travel is still per-example. The initial
+`reload_routes_unless_loaded` prevents lazy initialization from replacing the
+test routes when this group runs first or in isolation. No records are created
+in the route context hooks.
+
+Route reloading dropped from about 4.3% of the intermediate sampled profile to
+0.4% of the final profile. The group fell from 6.949s to 0.622s for the
+same 30 examples and remains independent of its execution order.
+
+### Routine request/SQL logs were work with no assertions
+
+`ActiveRecord::LogSubscriber#sql` accounted for about 7% of the baseline. No
+request examples assert logger output. Request execution now uses
+`Rails.logger.log_at(:warn)` to avoid formatting/writing debug/info logs while
+retaining warnings and errors. This is a block-scoped level, not a permanent
+change to application/test-environment configuration. SQL notifications remain
+active (covered by a regression example).
+
+Debugging opt-ins, including inherited/nested overrides:
+
+- `:verbose_logs`: debug logs, without SQL caller backtraces.
+- `:verbose_query_logs`: debug logs **and** SQL caller backtraces.
+- `verbose_logs: false`, `verbose_query_logs: false`: nested opt-outs.
+
+The logger level and SQL-backtrace setting are restored even after failures.
+The final profile has negligible SQL logging cost. The final profile still
+spends about 52% in fabrication, and webhook workers still run in integration
+cases (~3%). This remaining work belongs to the later factory phase; factories,
+password hashing, attachment processing and cryptography were not stubbed here.
+
+## Comparable result
+
+The same original **1,877 request examples** passed in **97.745s** with the same
+sampling settings and seed: **42.8% less execution time (1.75x as fast)** than
+170.953s. Wall time improved from 174.736s to 101.345s (42.0%).
+
+Combining **separately measured**, comparable sampled runs (never running both
+directories together):
+
+| Group | Original execution | Optimized execution |
+| --- | ---: | ---: |
+| Models (prior phase) | 157.576s | 62.045s |
+| Requests | 170.953s | 97.745s |
+| **Sum** | **328.529s** | **159.790s** |
+
+This meets the combined goal: **2.06x as fast / 51.4% less execution time**.
+Summed process wall time also more than halves: 335.598s -> 166.527s (2.02x).
+Models were not rerun in this phase; their recorded comparable result is reused.
+Absolute timings vary by machine, seed, profiler overhead and CI configuration.
+
+## Verification and future runs
+
+- Seed 12345, no profiler: **1,887 examples, 0 failures**, 95.069s execution.
+- Seed 67890 with isolation probes: **1,887 examples, 0 failures**, 94.206s.
+- The ten new `Request spec setup` examples cover fake/inline workers, nested
+  metadata overrides, clean queues, logging opt-ins, and active SQL notifications.
+- The signature group also passed alone: **30 examples, 0 failures**. This checks
+  lazy route loading when there are no preceding request groups.
+- Setup regression checks passed alone: **10 examples, 0 failures**.
+- Three deliberately failing examples (one cache-policy case, one signature
+  case, one verbose-SQL setup case) produced only the three injected failures,
+  with **zero errors outside examples**; the after-suite isolation checks still
+  passed. The same selection then passed without failure injection. One initial
+  probe selected only two cases because `--example` treats `^` literally; it was
+  corrected and is not counted as the three-case validation.
+- RuboCop passes for all changed/new Ruby files in this phase; shell syntax and
+  `git diff --check` pass.
+
+Reproduce the isolation checks without running any other spec type:
+
+```sh
+bundle exec rspec spec/requests --require ./docs/check_request_isolation.rb --seed 67890
+bundle exec rspec spec/requests --require ./docs/check_request_isolation.rb --example 'signature verification concern'
+bundle exec rspec spec/requests --require ./docs/check_request_isolation.rb --example 'Request spec setup'
+```
+
+The optional checker starts with global Sidekiq **inline**, SQL caller backtraces
+**enabled**, and logger level **INFO** to simulate incoming settings from other
+spec types. After each cache-matrix example it deliberately mutates a shared row;
+the next example must not see that mutation. After the suite it verifies original
+settings, rollback of the shared graph, restoration of real routes, and removal
+of the temporary controller. These probes are intentionally not default suite
+hooks. Seed 67890 emitted a Stoplight Redis clock-skew warning during the
+signature tests' existing time travel; it did not affect results.
+
+For the failure-path check, require an additional temporary Ruby file containing
+`RSpec.configure { |c| c.before(:each, type: :request) { raise 'intentional probe' } }`
+and select the following three full descriptions using repeated `--example`
+arguments (exit 1 is expected; check zero errors outside examples in RSpec JSON):
+
+- `Request spec setup when debugging SQL enables SQL caller backtraces`
+- `signature verification concern without a Signature header does not treat the request as signed`
+- `Caching behavior when anonymously accessed /users/alice redirects with proper cache header`
+
+Remaining hotspots for the factory phase include ActivityPub replies (~9.7s),
+grouped notifications (~7.2s), and notification setup (~4.7s). Permission shared
+examples often inherit their parent's substantial setup too (~10.5s aggregated
+at `spec/support/examples/api.rb`, not one request file). Shared-example JSON
+`file_path` points to the definition, so use the example `id` to attribute those
+costs to the including request file. Re-profile before changing these; preserve
+integration/negative assertions and do not replace real media or crypto work
+merely to obtain faster timings.
